{
  "id": "ALAS2-2026-4109",
  "title": "Amazon Linux 2 2017.12 - ALAS2-2026-4109: important priority package update for git",
  "issued": {
    "date": "2026-11-12 09:00:00"
  },
  "updated": {
    "date": "2026-11-12 09:00:00"
  },
  "severity": "important",
  "description": "Package updates are available for Amazon Linux 2 that fix the following vulnerabilities:\nCVE-2026-114469:\n\tBinary-patch size validation can be bypassed because it checks the encoded input rather than the inflated result, potentially causing an out-of-bounds read and crash.\n\nCVE-2026-114467:\n\tRemoving more than two GPG signatures from commit messages can corrupt stack memory, potentially causing denial of service during merges.\n\nCVE-2026-114466:\n\tCertain fast-import features can access arbitrary paths and are now disallowed by default.\n\nCVE-2026-113408:\n\tA server can advertise a malformed unborn HEAD, causing unintended file writes during subsequent ref updates with the files ref backend.\n\nCVE-2026-111760:\n\tRecursive clones can lead to remote code execution through unsafe handling of submodule-related repository metadata.\n\nCVE-2026-105437:\n\tSize calculations for very large merge results can overflow, leading to an undersized buffer and heap corruption.\n",
